pr_body:
Added missing support of DT gpio's "gpio_reserved_ranges" property. The array of pin range pairs as shown below now works. The implementation constraint is inherited from common DT stuff: a maximum of 64 pairs can be used, i.e. no more than 128-bit gpio ports are supported.

Usage example:
The reserved mask , defined in the device tree as:
gpio0: gpio0 {
....
ngpios=<32>;
gpio-reserved-ranges = <0 8>, <9 5>, <15 17>;
....
};

and used in driver configuration as:
{
...
.gpio_reserved_ranges = GPIO_RESERVED_PIN_MASK_FROM_DT_NODE(
DT_NODELABEL(gpio0)),
...
}

correctly converts to 0x80004100 (0b10000000000000000100000100000000)

Fixes #56999

